<!-- wp:wd/title {"blockId":"80425d00-cd9d-4484-9f17-af2646a770f4","content":"What we do","tpFontSize":"22"} -->
<h2 id="wd-80425d00" class="wp-block-wd-title title">What we do</h2>
<!-- /wp:wd/title -->

<!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"9bc40685-f928-49bf-8424-c0ac61ba80ba"} -->
<p id="wd-9bc40685" class="wp-block-wd-paragraph">Accept that it’s sometimes okay to focus just on the content or just on the design. Rigid proponents of content strategy may shun the use of dummy copy but then designers might want to ask them to provide style sheets with the copy decks they supply that are in tune with the design direction they require. Using dummy content or fake information in the Web design.</p>
<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:wd/column --></div>
<!-- /wp:wd/row -->

<!-- wp:wd/row {"blockId":"07afb7dc-a283-4e13-ac44-5b55af41cd08","marginBottom":"30"} -->
